Prov. 24:19   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Fret not yourself because of evildoers;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.1\"><span class=\"content\">be not </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 73:3; Prov. 3:31; 23:17; 24:1, 19</span></span><span class=\"content\">envious of wrongdoers!</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.1\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"content\">For they will soon </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Job 14:2; See Job 27:13-23 </span></span><span class=\"content\">fade like </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 90:5, 6 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the grass</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.2\"><span class=\"content\">and wither </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 129:6</span></span><span class=\"content\">like the green herb.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.2\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Ps. 62:8; 115:9-11; Prov. 3:5; Isa. 26:4   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Trust in the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">, and do good;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.3\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Lev. 26:5; Prov. 2:21  </span></span><span class=\"content\">dwell in the land and befriend faithfulness.</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">37:3 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">and feed on faithfulness</span><span class=\"ft\">, or </span><span class=\"fq\">and find safe pasture</span></span></span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.3\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Job 22:26; Isa. 58:14; [Phil. 3:1; 4:4]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Delight yourself in the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.4\"><span class=\"content\">and he will </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Matt. 6:33</span></span><span class=\"content\">give you the desires of your heart.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.4\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Ps. 22:8; 55:22; Prov. 16:3; 1 Pet. 5:7   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Commit your way to the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.5\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [See ver. 3 above]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">trust in him, and he will act.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.5\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Isa. 58:8, 10; Mic. 7:9   </span></span><span class=\"content\">He will bring forth your righteousness as the light,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.6\"><span class=\"content\">and your justice as </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Job 11:17</span></span><span class=\"content\">the noonday.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.6\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Ps. 62:1; Isa. 30:15; Lam. 3:26]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Be still before the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> and wait patiently for him;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.7\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    ver. 1   </span></span><span class=\"content\">fret not yourself over the one who </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Jer. 12:1</span></span><span class=\"content\">prospers in his way,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.7\"><span class=\"content\">over the man who carries out evil devices!</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.7\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Eph. 4:26]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Refrain from anger, and forsake wrath!</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.8\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [See ver. 7 above]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">Fret not yourself; it tends only to evil.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.8\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    ver. 2, 22   </span></span><span class=\"content\">For the evildoers shall be cut off,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.9\"><span class=\"content\">but those who wait for the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> shall </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 25:13; Prov. 2:21; Isa. 57:13; 60:21</span></span><span class=\"content\">inherit the land.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.9\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"content\">In </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Job 24:24 </span></span><span class=\"content\">just a little while, the wicked will be no more;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.10\"><span class=\"content\">though you look carefully at </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Job 7:10</span></span><span class=\"content\">his place, he will not be there.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.10\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"content\">But </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Cited Matt. 5:5 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the meek shall inherit the land</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.11\"><span class=\"content\">and delight themselves in </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 119:165; [Isa. 32:17]</span></span><span class=\"content\">abundant peace.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.11\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"content\">The wicked </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 31:13 </span></span><span class=\"content\">plots against the righteous</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.12\"><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Ps. 35:16</span></span><span class=\"content\">gnashes his teeth at him,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.12\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"content\">but the Lord </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Ps. 2:4 </span></span><span class=\"content\">laughs at the wicked,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.13\"><span class=\"content\">for he sees that his </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Job 18:20</span></span><span class=\"content\">day is coming.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.13\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"content\">The wicked draw the sword and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 7:12 </span></span><span class=\"content\">bend their bows</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.14\"><span class=\"content\">to bring down the poor and needy,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.14\"><span class=\"content\">to slay those whose </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Ps. 7:10</span></span><span class=\"content\">way is upright;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.14\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"content\">their sword shall enter their own heart,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.15\"><span class=\"content\">and their </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See 1 Sam. 2:4</span></span><span class=\"content\">bows shall be broken.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.15\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.16\"><span class=\"label\">16</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Prov. 15:16; 16:8; [1 Tim. 6:6]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">Better is the little that the righteous has</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.16\"><span class=\"content\">than the abundance of many wicked.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.16\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.17\"><span class=\"label\">17</span><span class=\"content\">For </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 10:15; Job 38:15; Ezek. 30:21, 22 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the arms of the wicked shall be broken,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.17\"><span class=\"content\">but the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 24</span></span><span class=\"content\">upholds the righteous.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.17\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.18\"><span class=\"label\">18</span><span class=\"content\">The </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Ps. 1:6 </span></span><span class=\"content\">knows the days of the blameless,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.18\"><span class=\"content\">and their </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 9</span></span><span class=\"content\">heritage will remain forever;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.18\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.19\"><span class=\"label\">19</span><span class=\"content\">they are not put to shame in evil times;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.19\"><span class=\"content\">in </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 33:19; Job 5:20</span></span><span class=\"content\">the days of famine they have abundance.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v19\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.19\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.20\"><span class=\"label\">20</span><span class=\"content\">But the wicked will perish;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.20\"><span class=\"content\">the enemies of the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> are like </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Matt. 6:30; James 1:11] </span></span><span class=\"content\">the glory of the pastures;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.20\"><span class=\"content\">they vanish&#8212;like </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 68:2; 102:3; Hos. 13:3</span></span><span class=\"content\">smoke they vanish away.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v20\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.20\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.21\"><span class=\"label\">21</span><span class=\"content\">The wicked borrows but does not pay back,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.21\"><span class=\"content\">but the righteous </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 26</span></span><span class=\"content\">is generous and gives;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v21\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.21\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.22\"><span class=\"label\">22</span><span class=\"content\">for those blessed by the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">37:22 </span><span class=\"ft\">Hebrew </span><span class=\"fq\">by him</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> shall </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ver. 9 </span></span><span class=\"content\">inherit the land,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.22\"><span class=\"content\">but those cursed by him </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 2</span></span><span class=\"content\">shall be cut off.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v22\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.22\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.23\"><span class=\"label\">23</span><span class=\"content\">The </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 25:12; 1 Sam. 2:9 </span></span><span class=\"content\">steps of a man are </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 40:2; 119:5</span></span><span class=\"content\">established by the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.23\"><span class=\"content\">when he delights in his way;</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v23\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.23\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.24\"><span class=\"label\">24</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Prov. 24:16; Mic. 7:8; 2 Cor. 4:9   </span></span><span class=\"content\">though he fall, he shall not be cast headlong,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.24\"><span class=\"content\">for the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 17</span></span><span class=\"content\">upholds his hand.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v24\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.24\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v25\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.25\"><span class=\"label\">25</span><span class=\"content\">I have been young, and now am old,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v25\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.25\"><span class=\"content\">yet I have not seen the righteous forsaken</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v25\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.25\"><span class=\"content\">or his children </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Ps. 109:10; Job 15:23]</span></span><span class=\"content\">begging for bread.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v25\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.25\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v26\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.26\"><span class=\"label\">26</span><span class=\"content\">He is ever </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 112:5, 9; Deut. 15:8, 10; Matt. 5:42; Luke 6:35</span></span><span class=\"content\">lending generously,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v26\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.26\"><span class=\"content\">and his children become a blessing.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v26\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.26\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v27\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.27\"><span class=\"label\">27</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    See Ps. 34:14   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Turn away from evil and do good;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v27\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.27\"><span class=\"content\">so shall you </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Ps. 102:28]</span></span><span class=\"content\">dwell forever.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v27\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.27\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.28\"><span class=\"label\">28</span><span class=\"content\">For the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Ps. 11:7 </span></span><span class=\"content\">loves justice;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.28\"><span class=\"content\">he will not forsake his </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Ps. 16:10 </span></span><span class=\"content\">saints.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.28\"><span class=\"content\">They are preserved forever,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.28\"><span class=\"content\">but the children of the wicked shall be </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 2, 9; Ps. 21:10; Prov. 2:22; Isa. 14:20</span></span><span class=\"content\">cut off.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v28\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.28\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v29\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.29\"><span class=\"label\">29</span><span class=\"content\">The righteous shall inherit the land</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v29\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.29\"><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[See ver. 27 above]</span></span><span class=\"content\">dwell upon it forever.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v29\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.29\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v30\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.30\"><span class=\"label\">30</span><span class=\"content\">The mouth of the righteous utters wisdom,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v30\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.30\"><span class=\"content\">and his tongue speaks justice.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v30\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.30\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v31\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.31\"><span class=\"label\">31</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Ps. 40:8; 119:11; Deut. 6:6; Isa. 51:7; Jer. 31:33; [Rom. 7:22]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">The law of his God is in his heart;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v31\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.31\"><span class=\"content\">his </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Ps. 73:2]</span></span><span class=\"content\">steps do not slip.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v31\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.31\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v32\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.32\"><span class=\"label\">32</span><span class=\"content\">The wicked </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 10:8</span></span><span class=\"content\">watches for the righteous</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v32\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.32\"><span class=\"content\">and seeks to put him to death.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v32\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.32\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v33\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.33\"><span class=\"label\">33</span><span class=\"content\">The </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> will not </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[2 Pet. 2:9] </span></span><span class=\"content\">abandon him to his power</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v33\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.33\"><span class=\"content\">or let him </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 109:31</span></span><span class=\"content\">be condemned when he is brought to trial.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v33\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.33\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v34\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.34\"><span class=\"label\">34</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    ver. 9; See Ps. 27:14   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Wait for the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> and keep his way,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v34\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.34\"><span class=\"content\">and he will exalt you to inherit the land;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v34\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.34\"><span class=\"content\">you will look on </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 52:5, 6; 91:8</span></span><span class=\"content\">when the wicked are cut off.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v34\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.34\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v35\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.35\"><span class=\"label\">35</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    See Job 5:3   </span></span><span class=\"content\">I have seen a wicked, ruthless man,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v35\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.35\"><span class=\"content\">spreading himself like </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Ps. 52:8]</span></span><span class=\"content\">a green laurel tree.</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">37:35 </span><span class=\"ft\">The identity of this tree is uncertain</span></span></span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v35\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.35\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v36\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.36\"><span class=\"label\">36</span><span class=\"content\">But he passed away,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">37:36 </span><span class=\"ft\">Or </span><span class=\"fq\">But one passed by</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> and behold, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 10; Job 20:5</span></span><span class=\"content\">he was no more;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v36\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.36\"><span class=\"content\">though I sought him, he could not be found.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v36\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.36\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v37\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.37\"><span class=\"label\">37</span><span class=\"content\">Mark the blameless and behold the upright,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v37\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.37\"><span class=\"content\">for there is a future for the man of </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ver. 11; Ps. 119:165; Isa. 57:2</span></span><span class=\"content\">peace.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v37\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.37\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v38\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.38\"><span class=\"label\">38</span><span class=\"content\">But </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Ps. 52:5; 104:35; Prov. 2:22] </span></span><span class=\"content\">transgressors shall be altogether destroyed;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v38\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.38\"><span class=\"content\">the future of the wicked </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 73:17; Job 18:17</span></span><span class=\"content\">shall be cut off.</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v38\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.38\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v39\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.39\"><span class=\"label\">39</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    See Ps. 3:8   </span></span><span class=\"content\">The salvation of the righteous is from the </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\">;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v39\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.39\"><span class=\"content\">he is their stronghold in </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 9:9</span></span><span class=\"content\">the time of trouble.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v39\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.39\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v40\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.40\"><span class=\"label\">40</span><span class=\"content\">The </span><span class=\"nd\"><span class=\"content\">Lord</span></span><span class=\"content\"> helps them and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Isa. 31:5; Acts 12:11] </span></span><span class=\"content\">delivers them;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v40\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.40\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [1 Chr. 5:20; Dan. 3:17, 28; 6:23]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">he delivers them from the wicked and saves them,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v40\" data-usfm=\"PSA.37.40\"><span class=\"content\">because they </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Ps. 11:1</span></span><span class=\"content\">take refuge in him.</span></span></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "next": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["PSA.38"], "human": "Psalm 38", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "previous": {"canonical": true, "usfm": ["PSA.36"], "human": "Psalm 36", "toc": true, "version_id": 59}, "reference": {"usfm": ["PSA.37"], "human": "Psalm 37", "version_id": 59}}, "usfm": "PSA.37.ASW", "locale": "en", "versionData": {"audio": true, "copyright_short": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers.</p>", "text": "The Holy Bible, English Standard Version\u00ae (ESV\u00ae), copyright \u00a9 2001 by Crossway, a publishing ministry of Good News Publishers."}, "id": 59, "language": {"iso_639_1": "en", "iso_639_3": "eng", "language_tag": "eng", "local_name": "English", "text_direction": "ltr"}, "local_abbreviation": "ESV", "local_title": "En